Version 1.1, 10 November 2026
Copyright RollingCodes

These are the terms for the Better Skill Creator repository at
https://github.com/rolling-codes/better-skill-creator
and for the v3.7.4 release. This file is the license. It does not include
any other license. The v3.7.4 downloads include this file.

1. Words

"The repository" means that GitHub repository at a commit that contains this
version of this file, including the source, docs, skill instructions, agent
prompts, tests, and scripts.

"A release download" means a file RollingCodes attaches to a GitHub release
of this repository. `skill-creator-3.7.4.skill` and
`better-skill-creator-plugin-3.7.4.zip` are release downloads. Each one
includes this file and is under it. The source archive for tag `v3.7.4`
includes this file and is under it.

"Sell" means taking money, a subscription, a fee, or anything else of value
for a copy, for access to a copy, or for a hosted service whose product is
the repository. Pay you receive for doing your job while you use the
repository yourself is not selling it. A price for a skill folder you wrote,
when that folder fails every test in section 4, is not selling the
repository.

"Post" means placing the files where someone other than you can download
them. A link to the official repository, with none of the files attached, is
not posting them.

A "word" is a run of letters or digits separated by whitespace. Counts below
ignore letter case. Line counts ignore blank lines and treat CRLF as LF.
Comments in Python, meaning a line whose first non-space character is `#`,
are removed before a source count.

2. What you may do

You may use the repository yourself, on your own computers, including a
computer you use for your job. You may study it. You may keep one private
copy and one private modification for that use.

You may use it to write a skill, a document, or another product that fails
every test in section 4. You may sell that product.

You may quote 15 words or fewer from one place in the repository, with the
name RollingCodes and the repository URL in the same paragraph.

You may sell an inspired product that passes every test in section 5.

3. What you may not do

You may not sell the repository, a release download, or a work that passes
any test in section 4.

You may not post the repository, a release download, or a work that passes
any test in section 4.

You may not give someone else permission to do either of those things.

4. The same product

A work is the same product when any one of these tests is true.

Test A. Release bytes.
The work contains `skill-creator-3.7.4.skill`,
`better-skill-creator-plugin-3.7.4.zip`, or a later release download from
this repository. Unzipping and zipping again still passes this test. Changing
the compression format still passes this test.

Test B. Repository tree.
The work contains a checkout of `rolling-codes/better-skill-creator`,
including a checkout with `.git` removed, or a zip, tar, or bundle of that
checkout. Deleting or renaming up to 10 files still passes this test.

Test C. Product name.
The name shown to a buyer or an installer is `Better Skill Creator`,
`better-skill-creator`, or `skill-creator-local`. The folder name
`skill-creator` passes this test when `SKILL.md` describes the folder as the
RollingCodes fork, or when `plugin.json` names the repository
`https://github.com/rolling-codes/better-skill-creator`.

Test D. Copied prose.
Forty or more words in a row from `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `SKILL.md`,
or any file in `docs/`, `agents/`, or `references/` appear in the work in the
same order. A quotation of 15 words or fewer, with the credit required in
section 2, does not pass this test.

Test E. Copied source.
Twenty or more non-blank lines in a row from `bsc.py` or from any `.py` file
in `skills/skill-creator/scripts/` appear in the work after comments are
removed and repeated whitespace is collapsed. Renaming variables does not
change the result when the other tokens still match in order.

Test F. Edited copy.
The work was made by starting from the repository and editing it. This
includes a fork, a branch, a translation of the files, a formatting pass, and
a patch. It also includes a tree in which at least 70 percent of the
non-blank lines in `skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md` are unchanged and at least
70 percent of the non-blank lines are unchanged in 5 or more files under
`skills/skill-creator/scripts/`.

Test G. Wrapper.
An installer, container, disk image, or paid download extracts, clones, or
fetches the repository or a release download, and the extracted tree passes
any of tests A through F.

These are the same product. Each one fails the license:

- A zip of the repository with the name changed to another product name.
- `SKILL.md` translated into another language and sold as a skill.
- A container whose command clones this repository.
- A fork that changes the version number, the badge color, or up to 10 files.
- The scripts with the comments removed and the functions renamed.

5. An inspired product you may sell

A product is inspired, and you may post it and sell it, only when every one
of these is true.

1. It fails tests A, B, C, D, E, F, and G.
2. You wrote its source files as new files. You may use these ideas: a skill
   is a folder containing `SKILL.md`; a program can check that folder; a
   program can grade saved files without calling a model; a program can pack
   a folder into an archive; a description can be revised from trigger
   results.
3. The product name is none of the names in test C, and the sales page does
   not say the buyer is getting Better Skill Creator.
4. It does not tell the buyer to download this repository or a release
   download as part of what they paid for.

Reusing the ordinary words `check`, `package`, and `eval` for those jobs does
not, by itself, pass test D or test E.

6. Credit

When you publish an inspired product, or when you use the 15-word quotation,
name RollingCodes and link to
https://github.com/rolling-codes/better-skill-creator

7. Name

This license does not let you use `Better Skill Creator`,
`better-skill-creator`, or `skill-creator-local` as the name of your product.

8. End of permission

If you sell or post a work that passes any test in section 4, the permissions
in section 2 end for you.

9. No warranty

The repository is provided as-is, without warranty of any kind.
